---
/**
 * The Modafied emblem, hotlinked (ADR-0013, revised).
 *
 * This component used to render a Modafied emblem from a JSON file stored in this repository.
 * That was wrong in a way worth recording, because it is the failure mode the whole arrangement
 * exists to prevent:
 *
 *   - A self hosted emblem is a frozen claim. Modafied's E2 says emblems are hotlinked and never
 *     handed over as files, precisely so a site cannot keep showing a flattering grade after the
 *     measurement moved. Our copies read "unrated" for five feeds Modafied had already graded
 *     A, B, and C.
 *   - We are not the issuer. Only Modafied can state a Modafied grade. A file in this repo saying
 *     issuer: "modafied" is Trooth putting words in the benchmark's mouth, and Trooth funds that
 *     benchmark, which is exactly when nobody should take our word for what it said.
 *
 * So the emblem is now a live reference to Modafied. Its embed script fetches the current
 * attestation and renders the emblem plus its trace id, which resolves to the scorecard digest
 * and method version behind the grade. If Modafied has never benchmarked the subject, its script
 * says so in its own words. If Modafied is unreachable, the slot degrades to a plain linked
 * emblem rather than blanking the page. In all of those cases the claim is Modafied's, not ours,
 * and we cannot freeze it, soften it, or invent it.
 *
 * Pages using this must also load the embed script once. Import MODAFIED_EMBED_SRC from
 * ../utils/modafied and render <script is:inline defer src={MODAFIED_EMBED_SRC}></script>.
 */
export interface Props {
  /** Subject id as Modafied catalogs it. Ours match, because both catalogs use the same ids. */
  subjectId: string;
  size?: "sm" | "md";
}

const { subjectId, size = "md" } = Astro.props;
---

<span
  class="emblem"
  data-modafied={subjectId}
  data-modafied-variant={size === "sm" ? "compact" : "full"}
></span>

<style>
  .emblem { display: inline-block; }
  /* The emblem arrives as a light SVG card; round it a little against a dark page. */
  .emblem :global(img) { border-radius: 6px; }
  .emblem :global(a) { text-decoration: none; }
</style>
